ation":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222156451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222561566","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/2498#issuecomment-1222561566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2498","id":1222561566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5I3s8e","user":{"login":"jlalmes","id":69924001,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTI0MDAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69924001?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes","html_url":"https://github.com/jlalmes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlalmes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-22T16:00:49Z","updated_at":"2022-08-22T16:00:49Z","body":"Additionally you lose the type-safety that you would expect from:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nt.procedure\r\n  .input(z.enum(['a', 'b']))\r\n  .input(z.literal('a'))\r\n  .query(({ input }) => {\r\n//           ^? junk equivalent to `string`\r\n  });\r\n``` \r\n\r\nEasy alternatives: \r\n\r\n- Override the last `input` parser added as the source of truth.\r\n- Allow only one `input` parser per procedure.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222561566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222564534","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/2498#issuecomment-1222564534","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2498","id":1222564534,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5I3tq2","user":{"login":"juliusmarminge","id":51714798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNzE0Nzk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51714798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge","html_url":"https://github.com/juliusmarminge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juliusmarminge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-22T16:03:01Z","updated_at":"2022-08-22T16:12:20Z","body":"> Hi @KATT, good job on this PR.\r\n> \r\n> I've given it a test and it seems to only suitable for the happy path (merging objects). The result of using any other primitives (string/number/array etc.) as input types seems to give an invalid and/or indecipherable input typing in the resolver function.\r\n> \r\n> Example: \r\n> ```ts\r\n> t.procedure\r\n>   .input(z.string())\r\n>   .input(z.string())\r\n>   .query(({ input }) => {\r\n> //           ^? junk\r\n>   });\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Would be great to have this feature, but I wander if the sheer volume of edge cases would push this outside of the tRPC scope at this time?\r\n> \r\n\r\nSorry @jlalmes edited your comment instead of quoting it xD\r\n\r\nNot sure what the expected output would be then? What keys would the different strings get?\r\n\r\nI think it's fair to assume if you want the object merged you gotta explicit name each key, ie. passing an object should be mandatory for chained inputs?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222564534/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1222593106","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/2498#issuecomment-1222593106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2498","id":1222593106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5I30pS","user":{"login":"KATT","id":459267,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTI2Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/459267?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT","html_url":"https://github.com/KATT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-22T16:22:55Z","updated_at":"